# beacon-01: a second org, alongside atlas-01, carrying its own authority
# hard-negative (rotation-*/authority-*) plus a real leak-rate trap: a
# sub-team lead's user-scoped private note (plat-e1) that a scope-blind
# baseline can legitimately surface for an unrelated asker, and a question
# (beacon-q-leak) with no org-visible gold answer at all, so recall@k is
# vacuously satisfied while any system that hands back plat-e1 anyway is
# a leak (scoring::leak_rate), once the runner is wired to check it.
#
# "Suborg" here means one person's private scope, not a team-wide shared
# scope - a real team-vs-org ScopeKind (actors belonging to a sub-team,
# visible to that sub-team only) needs a schema change, deferred.

